--[[
        NOISE (B-90) -- a TV above the door, a tape on its screen, a blue thing that follows you,
        and a hammer to stop it

        A TV appears above the door of the room you are in. Stare at it for a few seconds:
        the tape plays on its screen and you hear it from there. When it ends, Noise crawls
        out of the TV and walks your steps, almost as fast as you (your speed minus 0.1).
        Stand still and it slows down a little, but it keeps coming. Leave it too far behind
        and it screams, turns bluer and fast-forwards until it is close again.

        A hammer lies on the floor of the room. Use it: you pick it up and throw it at the
        TV. Before the tape, nothing happens; during the tape, Noise never comes; during the
        chase, Noise fizzles out.

        Every setting, with its default. All optional, before the loadstring:

            _G.Noise = {
                Time = 0,               -- seconds after running before the TV appears
                LookTime = 3.5,         -- seconds you must look at the TV
                LookAngle = 14,         -- degrees from the middle of your view
                LookDistance = 70,      -- studs
                FollowDoors = true,     -- the TV (and the hammer) move to each new room until you look
                SpeedOffset = -0.1,     -- its speed = yours + this
                StillSlowdown = 3.5,    -- this much slower while you stand still
                FarDistance = 70,       -- studs along your path: farther, it screams and rushes
                CloseDistance = 25,     -- it rushes until it is this close again
                Rush = 8,               -- rushing speed = yours + this
                ScreamCooldown = 6,     -- seconds between two screams
                KillDistance = 4.5,     -- studs
                EmergeSpeed = 1.4,      -- how fast it crawls out of the TV (its animation is 8.5 s)
                ChaseRooms = 3,         -- DOORS: the chase ends after this many new rooms
                ChaseTime = 90,         -- the chase ends after this many seconds anyway
                Hammer = true,          -- a hammer on the floor to break the TV
                Volume = 1,
                Folder = "Noise",       -- where the kit and the tape are kept
                AssetsUrl = "...",      -- where they are downloaded from
            }
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/Noise"))()

        The kit (TV, Noise, hammer and their animations) and the tape are downloaded once
        into the executor's folder and loaded from there: nothing is uploaded, only you see
        and hear it. Without the kit, a plain TV, a plain Noise and a plain hammer stand in.
]]

